both implement and composite the interface.

In proxy the client is unaware that the real subject is hidden from him. the proxy object looks like the real object.


In classic decorator the client *is* aware of the composition.


My take on this is:
<a> proxy is used to hide real subject from the client

<b> decorator is used to hide real subject from the server ( client can *add* functionality w/o
    the server knowing or caring ).


My thoughts reach out a bit and I would think the Chain of command is very similar to the decorator too
since its a sequence of decorators around the real object.

